1
00:00:07,049 --> 00:00:09,176
I've been meaning to talk with you.

2
00:00:09,968 --> 00:00:12,054
It's terrifying, isn't it?

3
00:00:13,471 --> 00:00:16,474
The president and I
have a simple request.

4
00:00:17,643 --> 00:00:19,311
Tell us what you see.

5
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:24,657
If anything in your environment
strikes you as a bit odd, a bit off,

6
00:00:24,692 --> 00:00:26,408
pick up the phone.

7
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:30,203
Whether it's a package or a
person that seems out of place,

8
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:32,032
we'd love you to let us know.

9
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:35,786
Because there's a lot of
noise out there these days.

10
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:39,129
A noisy press that's
choosing to dwell on the past

11
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:41,291
instead of what's happening right now.

12
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:44,419
My husband and I want to protect you.

13
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:48,138
In two weeks' time, you will
be heading to the ballot box

14
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:51,426
to decide what kind of
country you want to live in.

15
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:54,054
It's a profound choice.

16
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:59,567
But no matter who wins this election,
we're going to need to work together,

17
00:00:59,602 --> 00:01:01,443
watch out for each other,

18
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:04,029
and, yes, watch each other,

19
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:06,358
to keep us all safe and sound.

20
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:08,694
Tell us what you see.

21
00:01:09,612 --> 00:01:12,996
My name is Claire Underwood,
and I approve this message.

22
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,827
Should we do one more?

23
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:36,269
Did the Democrats show?

24
00:01:36,304 --> 00:01:38,814
They didn't disappoint.
Almost every member, sir.

25
00:01:38,849 --> 00:01:40,849
- Almost.
- I have a list of those who did.

26
00:01:40,851 --> 00:01:44,402
My fellow congressmen, I do
not need the Washington Herald

27
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:47,906
to tell me that a scoundrel
lives in the White House.

28
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,700
I can see the Democrats are here.

29
00:01:49,735 --> 00:01:51,862
They're eager to debate.

30
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:54,780
I say to the gentlemen on
the other side of the aisle...

31
00:01:54,782 --> 00:01:56,539
- thank you.
- Go.

32
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:58,792
Should we investigate the president

33
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,503
for crimes committed while
he was vice president?

34
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:04,422
I say, yes. Let's debate.

35
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:08,969
Let's debate this miscreant
all day and all night.

36
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,806
Madam Speaker. Parliamentary inquiry.

37
00:02:12,841 --> 00:02:14,090
The gentleman from Georgia

38
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:15,884
may state the nature of
his parliamentary inquiry.

39
00:02:15,886 --> 00:02:17,886
Do the rules of the House not require

40
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:20,105
the president be formally
invited in order to attend?

41
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,556
Madam Speaker, if I may...

42
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,642
The Speaker recognizes the
gentleman from South Carolina.

43
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:26,820
The president is wearing
his congressional pin today

44
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:29,907
and is thereby welcome to
any and all proceedings.

45
00:02:29,942 --> 00:02:32,325
Madam Speaker! Madam Speaker!

46
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,703
Rules of the House state

47
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:36,914
that former members are
not allowed on the floor

48
00:02:36,949 --> 00:02:38,999
when they have interest
in the matter under debate.

49
00:02:39,034 --> 00:02:40,500
Madam Speaker,

50
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:45,005
the president has no interest or opinion
on the matter being debated today.

51
00:02:46,709 --> 00:02:48,790
The House suspend.
The House will suspend.

52
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:53,180
Madam Speaker, I still do have the
floor, and I find it hard to believe

53
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:56,893
the president wouldn't have an
opinion on the matter being discussed.

54
00:02:56,896 --> 00:03:01,021
If the good gentleman from Florida
would yield a portion of his time,

55
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:05,643
I assure him it will satisfy his query.

56
00:03:08,856 --> 00:03:10,530
I yield three minutes to the leader.

57
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:14,451
And I yield my time to the former
congressman from South Carolina

58
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,954
and the President of the United States.

59
00:03:18,949 --> 00:03:22,327
Point of order! Parliamentary inquiry!

60
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,830
Parliamentary inquiry!

61
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:28,340
Parliamentary inquiry!

62
00:03:28,375 --> 00:03:30,550
Mr. President. This is beyond the norm.

63
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:32,004
I don't care.

64
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,340
I don't care.

65
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:41,436
And I also do not care about
your investigative committees.

66
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:45,517
No, that is not what I care about today.

67
00:03:46,393 --> 00:03:49,772
The House will cease.

68
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:55,235
That is not what I care about today.

69
00:03:56,862 --> 00:04:02,415
I am on my way to the funeral
of an American patriot.

70
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:06,789
A good man, a husband...

71
00:04:08,165 --> 00:04:13,211
a father... who was
beheaded on American soil.

72
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:19,141
And this chamber chooses to debate me?

73
00:04:20,177 --> 00:04:22,602
- The House will suspend.
- I asked to speak

74
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:26,648
to a full session of this chamber
and my requests were denied.

75
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:29,359
- Madam Speaker!
- Mr. President, you must yield the floor.

76
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:32,940
I will not yield, Madam Speaker.

77
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:35,991
Because I cannot wait.

78
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:42,532
One of the murderers...

79
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:49,462
One of the murderers who
killed Mr. Jim Miller...

80
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:51,506
is still out there.

81
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:53,251
At large.

82
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:58,680
How much more proof do you people need?

83
00:05:01,468 --> 00:05:06,188
I demand that every member
of this House take a stand.

84
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:09,983
Like FDR before, and Wilson before him.

85
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:12,194
I demand that this Congress

86
00:05:12,229 --> 00:05:18,033
declare a formal declaration of war
against ICO, both here and abroad.

87
00:05:18,068 --> 00:05:19,534
Motion to adjourn.

88
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:21,152
- Second!
- The House will adjourn.

89
00:05:21,154 --> 00:05:23,789
- The president will cease.
- I will not cease!

90
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:26,201
I will never cease.

91
00:05:26,784 --> 00:05:30,628
I demand that this Congress
declare a state of war

92
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:36,384
has existed and does exist between
ICO and the United States of America.

93
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:40,722
And I demand that every member
of this House stay in this chamber

94
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:45,602
for as long as it takes, until
you bring my request to a vote.

95
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:51,024
Or you will all go down
in history as cowards!

96
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,567
Cowards!

97
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,903
The sergeant at arms
will remove the president.

98
00:05:54,938 --> 00:05:58,531
Madam Speaker, I
repeat. I demand a vote.

99
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:00,277
I will not yield.

100
00:06:00,944 --> 00:06:03,328
I will not yield.

101
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:06,950
I will not yield.

102
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:35,143
- <font color="#D81D1D">Synced and corrected by VitoSilans</font> -
-- <font color="#138CE9">www.Addic7ed.com</font> --

103
00:07:44,131 --> 00:07:47,349
Alleged terrorist Zachary
Hawthorne was killed by the FBI,

104
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:50,185
but Joshua Masterson is still at large.

105
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:53,646
While the Miller family mourns, the
hunt for the missing terrorist continues

106
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:55,815
and tensions are running high.

107
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,775
The president may be asking for war,

108
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:01,321
but it seems war's already
been declared on him.

109
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,745
My fans.

110
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:19,422
FBI is looking into a multiple
shooting in Chattanooga.

111
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:22,127
- Reports have it gang related.
- No.

112
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:27,973
A private plane went down in
West Virginia. Mechanical failure.

113
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:30,100
A series of homes were
set on fire in Georgia,

114
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:31,476
most likely arson.

115
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:36,523
Uh... convenience store in North Carolina
exploded at about 4:00 in the morning.

116
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:39,734
- Where's the store?
- Uh, suburb outside of Raleigh.

117
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,604
The cause is still under investigation.

118
00:08:42,397 --> 00:08:45,365
- I'll make an appearance.
- Yes, ma'am.

119
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:48,118
Just put it on the schedule so
the media has time to mobilize.

120
00:08:48,153 --> 00:08:49,571
Yes, ma'am.

121
00:09:08,590 --> 00:09:12,059
I take it the president has
declared war on Joshua Masterson.

122
00:09:12,094 --> 00:09:14,221
He never should've
kicked me off that call.

123
00:09:15,222 --> 00:09:17,772
But this morning isn't about politics.

124
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,232
That's right.

125
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:22,194
We need to show some
compassion for the living.

126
00:09:22,229 --> 00:09:24,272
And respect for the dead.

127
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:32,245
The family's agreed to a moment.

128
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:35,325
No press, no speeches, but we
should be able to pull something.

129
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,037
- Mr. President.
- Governor.

130
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:47,052
Do they not realize what
we've done for them already?

131
00:09:47,087 --> 00:09:48,970
I pointed that out, sir, but...

132
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:51,514
the daughter's medicated and
very fragile at the moment.

133
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:52,550
All right.

134
00:09:54,136 --> 00:09:55,345
Mrs. Miller.

135
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:59,974
- I'm so very sorry.
- Thank you.

136
00:10:00,642 --> 00:10:01,941
And I promise you,

137
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:06,488
I will not stop until everyone
responsible for this terrible tragedy

138
00:10:06,523 --> 00:10:08,233
is brought to justice.

139
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:12,154
And I swear to you,
as God is my witness...

140
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:16,581
no one will ever harm you
or your family ever again.

141
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:20,627
The nation mourns with you
and your daughter, Mrs. Miller.

142
00:10:20,662 --> 00:10:24,207
- Thank you. If you don't mind...
- Of course.

143
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:31,673
Mr. President.

144
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:33,550
I'll be right along.

145
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:36,768
It's a busy day for you today, sir.

146
00:10:36,803 --> 00:10:39,264
It's a sad, sad day.

147
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:42,315
It's a shame things didn't
turn out differently.

148
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:46,354
Yes. Well, some things are
bigger than the two of us, Will.

149
00:10:51,193 --> 00:10:52,900
I don't want him here!

150
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,662
Calm down, Melissa. Please.

151
00:10:55,697 --> 00:10:58,080
It's his fault. He's dead.

152
00:10:58,115 --> 00:11:00,375
- Daddy's dead. He killed him.
- Please.

153
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:02,495
Give me a minute.

154
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:07,382
- Did you take your medicine?
- Yes. Okay? Yes.

155
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:08,585
Yes!

156
00:11:10,878 --> 00:11:15,300
You do. You think about what you
would say on a day like today.

157
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:18,261
If a day like today were to happen.

158
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:21,646
But you let it pass...

159
00:11:21,681 --> 00:11:24,982
because you know you have so
much more left ahead of you.

160
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:28,688
So much to do together.

161
00:11:30,232 --> 00:11:34,326
You think... You think 40 minutes...

162
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:37,954
If we were late 40 minutes...

163
00:11:37,989 --> 00:11:40,332
Or two, or one...

164
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:44,544
Or if we went somewhere else to eat...

165
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:50,627
But to dwell in the past,
to live in what-ifs...

166
00:11:52,337 --> 00:11:54,171
That wasn't my husband.

167
00:11:56,299 --> 00:11:57,509
That wasn't us...

168
00:11:59,302 --> 00:12:00,678
- Honey...
- Please.

169
00:12:01,721 --> 00:12:03,723
Okay. Come on.

170
00:12:07,519 --> 00:12:09,020
I need to...

171
00:12:13,483 --> 00:12:15,485
I wanted to say about my father...

172
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:21,991
He was so strong... so brave.

173
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:27,830
My father was taking us to...

174
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,502
My father...

175
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:36,638
- Come on, baby. It's okay.
- My father...

176
00:12:36,673 --> 00:12:39,801
You killed my father.
You're the reason he died.

177
00:12:40,677 --> 00:12:42,394
Melissa...

178
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:47,524
It's all right, Melissa. We understand.

179
00:12:47,559 --> 00:12:51,688
I hope you die and
she becomes president.

180
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,587
What did the girl say to you?

181
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:21,634
She said she hopes I die and
that you become the president.

182
00:13:29,976 --> 00:13:34,321
Mr. Macallan, this is Deputy
Director Michaels from the NSA.

183
00:13:34,356 --> 00:13:38,067
I'm literally in your office.
I believe we had a meeting.

184
00:13:41,363 --> 00:13:44,622
There's been raids as far up as
New York and down to the panhandle.

185
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:45,665
As of now,

186
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:49,544
Green's focusing in on the border
between Virginia and North Carolina.

187
00:13:49,579 --> 00:13:51,379
Seth has a statement
ready for this afternoon.

188
00:13:51,414 --> 00:13:53,255
No. The best statement is no statement.

189
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:56,293
Besides, I want Claire to be the
voice on this until we're ready.

190
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:57,920
Yes, sir.

191
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:01,723
- Quite a crowd out there.
- Well, we better bring Birch in first.

192
00:14:01,758 --> 00:14:03,015
Yes, sir.

193
00:14:03,050 --> 00:14:05,428
Congressman Birch.

194
00:14:06,971 --> 00:14:08,229
Bob.

195
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:11,483
Well, that was a little bit of
history this morning, wasn't it?

196
00:14:11,518 --> 00:14:13,860
- It certainly was.
- I couldn't see it any other way.

197
00:14:13,895 --> 00:14:15,403
No disagreement from here.

198
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:17,071
Well, you know how the Republicans are.

199
00:14:17,106 --> 00:14:18,615
Anything but a decision.

200
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:20,450
They mistake complaint for leadership.

201
00:14:20,485 --> 00:14:23,285
Well, instead of a
committee to investigate you,

202
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,365
you got one to discuss your declaration.

203
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,457
All the way to election day.

204
00:14:27,492 --> 00:14:29,501
Even if there's only a
handful of Republicans

205
00:14:29,536 --> 00:14:31,544
with the grit and
spit to put up a fight,

206
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:32,962
we can control the conversation.

207
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:36,048
Get them talking about anything
but that goddamn article.

208
00:14:36,083 --> 00:14:37,842
All right. Now, who from our side

209
00:14:37,877 --> 00:14:39,677
- do we need to massage?
- Womack.

210
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:43,055
The declaration caught him off
guard. Had to keep him out of it.

211
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:45,808
It's his constituents that
actually fight the damn thing.

212
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:48,686
Well, let's call in the
honorable gentleman from Missouri.

213
00:14:48,721 --> 00:14:51,766
- Oh, he's a bourbon man, isn't he?
- Yes, he is.

214
00:14:57,605 --> 00:15:01,949
- A stunt. Yes, I'm calling it a stunt.
- Charlie, if I may...

215
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:05,077
Tom, please, what are you implying?

216
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:10,041
This request for a declaration
of war is yet another distraction.

217
00:15:10,076 --> 00:15:12,877
And I've never been prouder of
the president than I am today.

218
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:15,672
I'm not denying what happened
to the Millers. It was a tragedy.

219
00:15:15,707 --> 00:15:18,508
No, but you are. Because
denying it is the tragedy.

220
00:15:18,543 --> 00:15:20,134
This is a pattern.

221
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:22,094
Your husband's
administration, Mrs. Underwood,

222
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:24,632
- continues to operate in the shadows.
- Tom...

223
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:28,685
I understand you believe in
the importance of your article.

224
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:32,098
And I agreed to come here today
and talk with you about it.

225
00:15:32,682 --> 00:15:35,518
But we're fighting to
keep this country safe.

226
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:41,280
Mrs. Underwood, the White House has
yet to release one piece of information

227
00:15:41,315 --> 00:15:45,284
about the attempted capture
of those domestic terrorists.

228
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:46,911
ICO terrorists, yes.

229
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:51,791
Reports from a few hours ago are
saying North Carolina or Virginia.

230
00:15:51,826 --> 00:15:54,126
But that's all we have.

231
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:56,629
Well, we are circling
in, we're getting closer.

232
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:58,255
I will tell you,

233
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:01,383
our intelligence community,
they are the real heroes.

234
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:04,471
Charlie, if we could get back to
my point, my sources confirmed...

235
00:16:04,506 --> 00:16:05,757
Tom.

236
00:16:06,466 --> 00:16:09,684
Heather Dunbar, no friend
of mine or my husband's,

237
00:16:09,719 --> 00:16:12,812
looked into these charges,
and cleared the president.

238
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:14,932
Cleared? Please.

239
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:19,151
The White House has not
had a single press briefing

240
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,612
since the Herald ran my article.

241
00:16:20,647 --> 00:16:23,239
You keep saying the White
House isn't speaking about this.

242
00:16:23,274 --> 00:16:25,276
I am sitting right here talking to you.

243
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:28,620
Not Remy Danton or Jackie Sharp.

244
00:16:28,655 --> 00:16:30,162
Or Lucas Goodwin, either.

245
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:33,249
- What?
- Excuse me. Lucas Goodwin, meaning?

246
00:16:33,284 --> 00:16:35,369
I'm saying, me. I'm here.

247
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:41,257
And I don't know how many more
times we have to go over this.

248
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:44,135
You know, a Tom Hammerschmidt
article used to be

249
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:47,924
the first thing I would look for
when I opened the Washington Herald.

250
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:50,642
The Underwoods are
no longer campaigning.

251
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:52,810
They can call it what they want.

252
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:55,897
Well, if you think about the last
few days, what's in the air...

253
00:16:55,932 --> 00:17:00,151
It might not be such a bad idea for
us to take it one handshake at a time.

254
00:17:00,186 --> 00:17:01,896
Or call it for what it is.

255
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:04,405
"Home and abroad."

256
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,824
The president is essentially
asking for permission

257
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:09,451
- to fight a war on our soil.
- We can't push back too hard.

258
00:17:09,486 --> 00:17:10,945
We can't afford to look soft on terror.

259
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:13,080
We can't look the other way, either.

260
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:16,501
You of all people know where
this kind of talk leads.

261
00:17:16,536 --> 00:17:19,330
...ICO and the United States of America.

262
00:17:20,075 --> 00:17:22,623
Make sure the committee dealing
with the declaration of war

263
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:24,210
never gets to a vote.

264
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:28,590
We're not against
war, we're against his.

265
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,381
And I want you to
reach out to the Speaker

266
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:33,304
and find out who she's
putting on that committee.

267
00:17:34,345 --> 00:17:36,604
We need to get back to
the president's crimes.

268
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:39,183
That's the story. It's the only story.

269
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:42,436
Anything else?

270
00:17:43,563 --> 00:17:45,071
I have my script.

271
00:17:45,106 --> 00:17:47,740
I will not yield!

272
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:49,277
I will not...

273
00:17:58,535 --> 00:17:59,621
Harry...

274
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:04,340
I want to know what he
says and when he says it.

275
00:18:04,375 --> 00:18:06,335
Our general isn't used to taking orders.

276
00:18:07,169 --> 00:18:08,671
Will, one more thing.

277
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,759
- What?
- Your wife.

278
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,935
Okay, I know we opened up
this campaign on Pollyhop,

279
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:19,724
but it might be time to close it
down... or at least be more careful.

280
00:18:20,767 --> 00:18:22,692
Well, what did they find out?

281
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:26,237
The home of the mother of the terrorist,
you know, the one they're looking for,

282
00:18:26,272 --> 00:18:28,030
was vandalized last night.

283
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:31,367
Garage set on fire. Broken windows.

284
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:33,535
And, uh, Hannah...

285
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:36,163
well... she posted.

286
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:38,284
She was defending the mother online.

287
00:18:41,287 --> 00:18:43,630
- When?
- This afternoon.

288
00:18:43,665 --> 00:18:46,250
The timing is not good on this.

289
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:49,295
- I can show you.
- Not now.

290
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:54,932
Thank you.

291
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:57,685
Governor Conway and I
are honored to be here

292
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:00,897
with the Miller family
and their closest friends.

293
00:19:00,932 --> 00:19:04,769
I know the VFW was a big part
of Jim's life here in Knoxville.

294
00:19:05,728 --> 00:19:07,612
With the help of
Homeland and our hotline,

295
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:10,698
we think that Masterson has crossed
into the southwest corner of Virginia.

296
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:12,568
Scott or Washington.

297
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,113
- And?
- And...

298
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:19,033
Assistant Director Green?

299
00:19:19,742 --> 00:19:23,502
We're relying on aerial support,
sightings and local law enforcement.

300
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:24,629
But we're fairly confident

301
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:27,048
we can have him pinned
down in the next 24 hours.

302
00:19:27,083 --> 00:19:29,508
The president wants us
to be absolutely sure.

303
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:33,089
We can't have him getting away
again. Careers are at stake.

304
00:19:33,715 --> 00:19:37,433
Everyone around this table is fully
aware of the gravity of the situation.

305
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:40,596
Good. The president will
be happy to hear that.

306
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:57,054
Okay. What kind of kiss do you want?

307
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,716
- Eskimo.
- In...

308
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:02,428
and out.

309
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:05,514
I'll be right back.

310
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:17,651
- You're angry.
- I am.

311
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:22,663
I was asked a question and I answered.

312
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,325
That's the least of it.

313
00:21:25,827 --> 00:21:28,377
Okay, well, I don't want
to talk about it right now.

314
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:31,213
Are you trying to lose
this election? Are you?

315
00:21:31,248 --> 00:21:32,924
Oh, Will, stop it.

316
00:21:32,959 --> 00:21:37,636
This woman that you're defending...
Her son just cut someone's head off.

317
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:39,305
And he's still out there somewhere.

318
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,381
- Do you understand what this looks like?
- Stop it.

319
00:21:41,884 --> 00:21:44,393
Do you want to know
why our son can't sleep?

320
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:46,472
He's eight years old,
and he can't sleep.

321
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:49,141
Because he's having nightmares.

322
00:21:49,934 --> 00:21:53,820
Because he thinks there's a big
black dog running around the hotel.

323
00:21:53,855 --> 00:21:55,154
- Dog?
- Yes.

324
00:21:55,189 --> 00:21:58,032
He closes his eyes, and
he can hear it growling.

325
00:21:58,067 --> 00:22:00,027
He's scared, Will.

326
00:22:05,116 --> 00:22:09,829
I said what I said because
that woman is a victim.

327
00:22:10,913 --> 00:22:12,289
We all are.

328
00:22:13,124 --> 00:22:14,750
And it has to stop.

329
00:22:20,006 --> 00:22:21,798
I want you to win.

330
00:22:24,426 --> 00:22:26,678
Get yourself a drink.
I'll be right back.

331
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:46,115
That's the mother. And
this is Hannah's response.

332
00:22:47,033 --> 00:22:50,667
She's not a criminal and should not
be punished for the sins of her son.

333
00:22:50,725 --> 00:22:53,610
We all, I know, reject the rhetoric

334
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:57,008
and actions of these
damaged, troubled young men.

335
00:22:57,043 --> 00:23:00,177
What I mean is, this is
a time for reflection,

336
00:23:00,212 --> 00:23:01,262
not aggression...

337
00:23:01,297 --> 00:23:04,265
So she's not condoning
it, but it is sympathetic.

338
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:06,017
Plays into the idea
that Joshua and Zachary

339
00:23:06,052 --> 00:23:08,477
were just a pair of troubled
kids looking for a cause,

340
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:10,722
no different than some school shooter.

341
00:23:11,682 --> 00:23:14,268
The post has been shared
over 100,000 times.

342
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:17,563
I want to talk with her.

343
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,656
- Hannah?
- The mother.

344
00:23:20,691 --> 00:23:24,576
We've been very careful
about where you appear.

345
00:23:24,611 --> 00:23:27,906
- LeAnn, will you excuse us for a moment?
- Of course.

346
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:37,714
We need to dial up the terror.

347
00:23:37,749 --> 00:23:39,508
And the mother can help us with that.

348
00:23:39,543 --> 00:23:42,463
But that also means we
have to locate Masterson.

349
00:23:42,945 --> 00:23:44,238
Soon.

350
00:23:49,345 --> 00:23:50,972
Tom is waiting for me.

351
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,099
Well, you go on.

352
00:24:00,982 --> 00:24:02,191
Francis...

353
00:24:03,900 --> 00:24:06,487
I shouldn't have cried at the funeral.

354
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:11,283
- No, it played beautifully.
- Not for me.

355
00:24:15,496 --> 00:24:16,663
Come with me.

356
00:24:18,499 --> 00:24:20,126
Come on. Just tell him you'll be late.

357
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:29,808
- Mr. President.
- It's all right, Officer.

358
00:24:29,843 --> 00:24:30,886
Ma'am.

359
00:24:33,055 --> 00:24:35,147
May I have your scope?

360
00:24:35,182 --> 00:24:38,144
Scope on your gun. I
promise I'll give it back.

361
00:24:43,690 --> 00:24:45,484
Thank you. Come here.

362
00:24:57,454 --> 00:25:00,916
Now, if you just hold the scope
a little a ways from your face...

363
00:25:01,417 --> 00:25:06,213
and look down, straight down,
across the lawn... right to the gate.

364
00:25:11,302 --> 00:25:13,679
- You see them?
- Hmm.

365
00:25:14,846 --> 00:25:19,310
Those people want a voice.
Some for, some against.

366
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:23,814
And they're looking back across the lawn,
toward this house and these windows...

367
00:25:24,981 --> 00:25:26,948
and they're thinking,

368
00:25:26,983 --> 00:25:30,821
"I wonder what the president and
the First Lady are doing tonight.

369
00:25:31,572 --> 00:25:34,200
And will they be able to protect us?"

370
00:25:37,328 --> 00:25:38,829
I should have been there.

371
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:41,547
Where?

372
00:25:41,582 --> 00:25:45,008
When you got shot. I wish I was there.

373
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:46,545
Maybe I could've...

374
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:49,215
protected you.

375
00:25:54,178 --> 00:25:56,263
You see, all those people want...

376
00:25:57,055 --> 00:26:01,102
is someone to keep them from
what they're afraid to know.

377
00:26:05,981 --> 00:26:09,735
And what are the president and
First Lady doing tonight, Francis?

378
00:26:10,361 --> 00:26:12,988
Well, I believe Thomas
is waiting for you.

379
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,033
Thank you, sir.

380
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:21,519
I'll see you in the morning.

381
00:26:25,251 --> 00:26:26,793
Do you have a smoke?

382
00:26:32,924 --> 00:26:34,135
Thank you.

383
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:43,059
♪ I know what my people
are thinking tonight ♪

384
00:26:44,561 --> 00:26:48,690
♪ As home through the
shadows they wander ♪

385
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:53,237
♪ Everyone smiling
in secret delight ♪

386
00:26:54,029 --> 00:26:56,907
♪ As they stare at
the castle and ponder ♪

387
00:26:58,242 --> 00:27:00,869
♪ And whenever the
wind blows this way ♪

388
00:27:01,787 --> 00:27:04,373
♪ You can almost hear everyone say ♪

389
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:09,211
♪ I wonder what the
king Is doing tonight ♪

390
00:27:17,678 --> 00:27:19,555
I've been looking for you.

391
00:27:20,597 --> 00:27:21,848
I got hungry.

392
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,226
So I went down to the main kitchen.

393
00:27:24,935 --> 00:27:27,110
That's a lovely group of
people you have down there.

394
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:29,898
If there's anything you
need, it can be brought up.

395
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:33,319
I didn't know what I needed
until I was eating it.

396
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:36,322
I heard the president's declaration.

397
00:27:37,573 --> 00:27:38,699
Very compelling.

398
00:27:44,079 --> 00:27:45,289
What did you really think?

399
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:48,209
It was almost like the real thing.

400
00:28:07,018 --> 00:28:09,861
The NSA has good people. Very good.

401
00:28:09,896 --> 00:28:12,239
- Too good.
- Not as good as you.

402
00:28:12,274 --> 00:28:14,032
Good enough to find my algorithms.

403
00:28:14,067 --> 00:28:16,410
That doesn't mean they knew
what we were using them for.

404
00:28:16,445 --> 00:28:17,828
No, no.

405
00:28:17,863 --> 00:28:20,121
One second, they send me
home, and then the next,

406
00:28:20,156 --> 00:28:21,998
they tell me, "Come back!"

407
00:28:22,033 --> 00:28:26,044
- They'll been watching me. This is a trap.
- Or the only way out.

408
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:27,379
God damn it.

409
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,375
- You want out?
- Don't you?

410
00:28:32,669 --> 00:28:33,670
LeAnn...

411
00:28:36,757 --> 00:28:38,925
we have done some illegal things here.

412
00:28:40,344 --> 00:28:41,560
There are other campaigns.

413
00:28:41,595 --> 00:28:44,771
- If you can get into the NSA...
- That's not possible.

414
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:46,940
Into their system, you can fix this.

415
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:48,644
- You're not listening to me.
- I am.

416
00:28:50,354 --> 00:28:52,063
I know the Underwoods.

417
00:28:53,106 --> 00:28:56,575
The only way that we
are gonna survive this...

418
00:28:56,610 --> 00:28:57,861
is if they win.

419
00:28:59,905 --> 00:29:01,990
You can help them win.

420
00:29:02,658 --> 00:29:04,243
I know you can.

421
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:19,341
I got on the paper right
around the time you left.

422
00:29:19,841 --> 00:29:21,808
Did you start in Style?

423
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:23,184
Metro desk.

424
00:29:23,219 --> 00:29:25,479
But then I did this
piece, a street fashion,

425
00:29:25,514 --> 00:29:26,932
kids on the street thing.

426
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:30,651
I'm surprised you asked for me.

427
00:29:30,686 --> 00:29:33,522
Some people are being moved
around and off the team.

428
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:39,152
The Masterson story.
"War, what is it good for?"

429
00:29:43,156 --> 00:29:46,333
Were you ever interested
in investigative journalism?

430
00:29:46,368 --> 00:29:48,829
If you ask me, if it's not
investigating, it's not journalism.

431
00:29:52,874 --> 00:29:56,169
Word around here is you can
get anybody to talk to you.

432
00:29:58,672 --> 00:30:01,383
After 8:00, with a
drink in their hands...

433
00:30:02,468 --> 00:30:03,469
yeah.

434
00:30:12,519 --> 00:30:14,980
She's the one they say you called a...

435
00:30:16,982 --> 00:30:17,983
you know.

436
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:23,329
I'm sorry. I'm a little nervous.

437
00:30:23,364 --> 00:30:27,368
You're sort of a legend and...
articles on the president?

438
00:30:29,202 --> 00:30:31,204
It'd be an honor to work
with you in any capacity.

439
00:30:32,873 --> 00:30:34,458
To be part of this.

440
00:30:38,253 --> 00:30:41,388
Did you find him? Did you?

441
00:30:41,423 --> 00:30:43,432
It'll only be another moment.

442
00:30:43,467 --> 00:30:45,809
Because I've done all I can.

443
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:48,472
Everything you told
me to. You know that.

444
00:30:49,348 --> 00:30:51,057
They know that, don't they?

445
00:30:54,770 --> 00:30:55,771
Mrs. Underwood.

446
00:30:57,398 --> 00:31:00,901
I was hoping to speak to Ms. Masterson.

447
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:04,070
Just the two of us.

448
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:27,553
Is there a problem?

449
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,930
It is a bit extreme.

450
00:31:31,139 --> 00:31:34,107
Expanding the no-fly
list to this extent.

451
00:31:34,142 --> 00:31:38,274
The restrictions on visas alone is
unprecedented. How do we justify?

452
00:31:38,277 --> 00:31:40,021
The White House counsel's
been all through that.

453
00:31:40,023 --> 00:31:41,615
It's there in black and white.

454
00:31:41,650 --> 00:31:43,992
We're virtually closing down our borders

455
00:31:44,027 --> 00:31:46,828
- without any hard evidence to back it up.
- It's coming.

456
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:50,081
A lot of innocent people are
trying to get into this country.

457
00:31:50,116 --> 00:31:51,868
They could be hurt by this.

458
00:31:54,871 --> 00:31:58,882
A change in policy this
big, I want it done right.

459
00:31:58,917 --> 00:32:02,135
I want you to let the world know

460
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:05,556
that if they want to continue coming
to this country for our hospitals,

461
00:32:05,591 --> 00:32:09,560
our colleges, our golf courses
and God knows what else...

462
00:32:09,595 --> 00:32:14,057
they're going to have to deliver more
than my head on the end of a burning stick.

463
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:19,277
Now look, Cathy, I know you have
well-earned relationships out there.

464
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:20,446
Long-standing.

465
00:32:20,481 --> 00:32:23,114
I'm not holding back,
Francis. I have reached out.

466
00:32:23,149 --> 00:32:26,660
Then I need you to reach further.
I want actionable intelligence.

467
00:32:26,695 --> 00:32:28,829
I want to know where ICO
is, or at the very least,

468
00:32:28,864 --> 00:32:30,914
that everyone's out there looking.

469
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,373
Are we clear?

470
00:32:32,408 --> 00:32:33,459
We're clear.

471
00:32:33,494 --> 00:32:35,579
Thank you, Cathy. I know
you won't let me down.

472
00:32:45,631 --> 00:32:46,632
He's dead.

473
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:50,391
- Is that why you're here?
- We're still looking for him...

474
00:32:50,426 --> 00:32:53,764
Because if he's dead, I want
to see him. To touch him.

475
00:32:56,141 --> 00:32:57,190
I'm trying to help...

476
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:59,568
- Ms. Masterson, please.
- But he hasn't contacted me.

477
00:32:59,603 --> 00:33:02,147
- I wish he would.
- I understand. Calm down.

478
00:33:04,608 --> 00:33:08,153
He's not a monster like they all say.

479
00:33:09,530 --> 00:33:12,783
- I lost him somewhere.
- But he's not...

480
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:17,746
But still, monsters
do exist, don't they?

481
00:33:23,209 --> 00:33:24,545
I want my lawyer.

482
00:33:26,630 --> 00:33:27,839
What for?

483
00:33:32,177 --> 00:33:34,185
I'm sorry, I don't know why I said that.

484
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:36,723
I don't know why I say anything anymore.

485
00:33:39,059 --> 00:33:43,605
I wanted to see you... to
ask you a simple question.

486
00:33:44,690 --> 00:33:48,026
Didn't you know what was
going on in your home?

487
00:33:49,528 --> 00:33:51,995
- Excuse me?
- You knew...

488
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:54,122
even before he went to Pakistan.

489
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:56,702
- I mean, you raised him.
- No.

490
00:33:57,994 --> 00:34:01,081
No. He had some problems. He got lost.

491
00:34:01,748 --> 00:34:05,335
- But no, nothing like this.
- But you saw what he did, didn't you?

492
00:34:09,590 --> 00:34:11,431
- No.
- Would you like to see it?

493
00:34:11,466 --> 00:34:14,142
We can show it to you, if you like.

494
00:34:14,177 --> 00:34:15,846
No. Please don't.

495
00:34:23,895 --> 00:34:27,148
What he did to that
family, to that man...

496
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:31,361
What sort of person
would do such a thing?

497
00:34:32,738 --> 00:34:35,866
He's my son.

